            <ArticleTitle>Death caused by simultaneous subacute stent thrombosis of sirolimus-eluting stents in left anterior descending artery and left circumflex artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e8-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ijcard.2008.11.035</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Simultaneous drug-eluting stent thrombosis in multivessel disease is a low incidence, but could cause lethal clinical event. We report a case with death caused by simultaneous subacute stent thrombosis of sirolimus-eluting stents in the proximal left anterior descending artery and in the proximal left circumflex artery.</AbstractText>
